{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CHKh4AmJg1uXLXJBic3inv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-folder personal productivity + R&D mission-control system for J.C. Liechty. Grounded from the project docs:\n\n- **What it is:** A self-contained, stdlib-only Python app (`anchor_gui.py`) that runs as a persistent local web server (NSSM service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`) and serves an interactive browser dashboard. It reads and writes plain-markdown files directly â€” no database, no external dependencies (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n\n- **Core purpose (productivity):** A GTD-style task/project manager. Markdown files are the source of truth (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, per-domain files under `domains/`). It supports a full task lifecycle â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” editable both in the browser and via the `anchor.py` CLI mirror.\n\n- **Second purpose (R&D control surface):** A \"Project Cockpit\" for trio-driven R&D work â€” the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill pipeline. Each project window shows lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass Catchers) as tiles with one honest status light (green/amber/red/grey), each expanding an inline panel with a cached summary plus a real, resizable terminal.\n\n- **What it ships under the hood:** Real ConPTY interactive terminals (`pty_manager.py`/`terminal_session.py` over xterm.js + a hand-rolled WebSocket), per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), cached/validated session+project summaries, stage handoffs, deliverable pin/declare/launch-by-type, and ephemeral deliverable previews (hard-guarded never to bind port 8777).\n\n- **Reliability:** A daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every markdown file, exercises every endpoint and the full task lifecycle, and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, never touching the real `:8777` service or real data), writing a dated report.\n\n- **Branding/lineage:** Presented as a Ghost World Labs tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\" The R&D surface has shipped through v4 (\"Project Cockpit,\" 9 waves green, merged to master).\n\nNote: the current branch is `foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit` with uncommitted work in progress (a \"v4.1\" iteration on the cockpit), so the live code is slightly ahead of what CLAUDE.md documents as merged."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e37781b-883c-4d48-a3cc-b07208cff2e0","uuid":"a298d0ed-ba43-4e18-83b2-30dc3fcbf379","request_id":"req_011Cc1oE2NXnJDpCerVD7DiC"}
